# Public origin of the deployed site, used to build canonical and Open Graph URLs.
# Example: https://www.aura-soli.online
# When empty, no canonical or og:url tags are emitted (no domain is assumed).
# Set this (and the EmailJS values below) in the Vercel project environment too.
VITE_SITE_URL=

# EmailJS — client-side contact form delivery.
# 1. In the EmailJS dashboard, create/select an Email Service (Services tab)
#    and copy its Service ID into VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID.
# 2. Copy the Public Key (Account > General) into VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY.
# 3. Create a template using the variables `from_name`, `reply_to`, `company`,
#    `service`, `budget`, and `project_details`, then copy its ID into
#    VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID.
# Never store the EmailJS Private Key in any browser-side env file or source.
# Private Key is not needed for the client-side `send` flow.
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=your_emailjs_public_key
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=your_emailjs_service_id
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=your_emailjs_template_id
